;; mesh-map (FEAT-018 S-B) — scatter + gather fused: the 90% fan-out.
;;
;; Spawn one await-free child per item (uniform shared prefix + region), then
;; await them all and return the results in order. The common parallel-map over a
;; collection of missions. Composes the two primitives directly (no new mechanism)
;; so it stays the same await-free shape FEAT-011 ships.
;;
;; Capacity-safe (BUG-020): the spawn step is `psettled`, so an item whose spawn
;; hits parallel_capacity_exceeded settles as {"err" reason} in place rather than
;; aborting the whole fan-out and orphaning the children that already spawned. The
;; await step skips the err markers and passes them through, so the result list is
;; one entry per item (results + per-item error markers), never a lost child.
;;
;; Args (data/*):
;;   items           — the collection to map missions over (required).
;;   prompt          — shared prompt prefix; each child gets (str prompt item).
;;   region          — the shared region the cohort coordinates in.
;;   tools           — optional capability subset for every child.
;;   inherit-memory  — optional uniform def-env slice for every child.
;;
;; Returns [result | {"err" ...} ...] — the awaited result of each item's child,
;; in order, with a settled error marker for any item that could not spawn.
(let [entries (map (fn [settled] (unwrap-or settled settled))
                   (psettled (fn [item]
                               (tool/spawn-session {:prompt (str data/prompt item)
                                                    :region data/region
                                                    :tools data/tools
                                                    :inherit-memory data/inherit-memory}))
                             data/items))]
  (map (fn [entry]
         (if (err? entry)
           entry
           (tool/await-session {:handle entry})))
       entries))
